  "correction": {
    "one_sentence": "A self-shield rider whose payload declares rebind_on_ability_hit now moves, inside the survival walk, to the first ability packet its holder lands instead of dying with the carrier it was bound to by ordinal, so catalyst_roster's Malphite is granted Granite Shield at 7.49 and its denial receipt is replaced by an applied shield, while liandry_reprice_mage_roster's Malphite lands no candidate at all and gains the denial row that names the last one.",
    "why_the_new_numbers_are_right": "Granite Shield is granted on Malphite's ability landing, which only the walk can settle: the Q it was authored on is attacker_state_blocked, his ability against ally:Pantheon lands at 7.49, and in game that hit grants the shield. The 243.3 is the same amount the rider always carried and the 217.8 absorbed is what the roster deals him in the 8 s the shield holds. liandry_reprice_mage_roster moves no number: Malphite is blocked through every in-window candidate there, so the rider stays refused and only the receipt naming that fact is new.",
    "pair_jurisdiction": "champions/slotlib.attach_self_shield stamps rebind_on_ability_hit on the payload it writes, so every module authoring a self shield gains one boolean leaf in the pair snapshot. No number moves in that jurisdiction."
  },
